<<<
only. 3. However too late. These extravagant German counter-attacks in mass on the Cambrai front, however, materially helped the French operations in Champagne. The excuse
===
only.

**3. *However* too late.** *These extravagant German counter-attacks in mass on the Cambrai front,* however, *materially helped the French operations in Champagne.* The excuse
>>>

<<<
the conjunction —that these ... front is in effect a single word—is sound only against a suggestion that it should be placed after attacks; it, or Nevertheless, or All the same, could have stood
===
the conjunction —that *these . . . front* is in effect a single word—is sound only against a suggestion that it should be placed after *attacks*; it, or *Nevertheless*, or *All the same*, could have stood
>>>

